+\revision{\mbox{\tabref{tab:ablation-edid}} reports the results of these supplementary ablation evaluations. The best-observed image-level Final scores are 52.16 for ResNet50, 53.75 for ResNet50+DFE, 53.27 for ResNet50+ARC, and 55.42 for the joint model. The joint configuration improves Final by 3.26 points over the baseline and by 1.67 and 2.15 points over the DFE and ARC configurations, respectively. It achieves the highest Final in both the ODIR Off-site and external EDID ablations, supporting the value of the joint configuration for cross-dataset recognition.}
+
+The \revision{ODIR Off-site} ablation results show that Adaptive Label-Feature Relevance Construction (ARC) improves label relevance modeling in multi-disease co-occurrence scenarios, while Dual-Branch Guided Domain-Invariant Feature Extraction (DFE) supports learning domain-invariant features from a single source domain when multi-institutional joint training is restricted. The integration of the two modules further improves multi-label recognition performance under single-source-domain training and provides a basis for the subsequent cross-domain generalization results.
 
